# The recorded rename map from the mini baseline (.flow/tmp/scala-dsl/mini-selected-baseline-00d22597d2)
# to the tree, read by make model-check-changed (model/temporal/check/Coverage.scala). A task that renames a
# machine, a table or an action of activity_mini or the shared code appends its entries here.
#
# fn-160.3 step-table rename map (old new): machines renamed into their family prefix (fn-160 R7).
# activity_mini (family answer, facet dispatching, family queue)
temporal.features.activity.mini.protocol.trustingAnswers temporal.features.activity.mini.protocol.answerTrusting
temporal.features.activity.mini.protocol.dispatchProgress temporal.features.activity.mini.protocol.dispatchingProgress
temporal.features.activity.mini.protocol.scheduledQueue temporal.features.activity.mini.protocol.queueScheduled
# shared task queue foundation (family queue)
temporal.foundations.taskqueue.protocol.forgetfulQueue temporal.foundations.taskqueue.protocol.queueForgetful
temporal.foundations.taskqueue.protocol.lossyMatchingQueue temporal.foundations.taskqueue.protocol.queueLossyMatching
temporal.foundations.taskqueue.protocol.volatileQueue temporal.foundations.taskqueue.protocol.queueVolatile
# the composition member a composition table names by its machine's short name
scheduledQueue queueScheduled
# fn-169.1 IR type-name rename map (ir old new): the authoring DSL moved from package framework
# into framework.dsl, and the IR names the DSL's types by their package (owner, 2026-10-12). The
# step tables name none of them, so a steps-only comparison leaves them to the IR; the mini lift
# equals the one before the move under them (framework/check/equivalence/Lifts.scala).
ir framework.Step framework.dsl.Step
ir framework.outcomes.Outcome framework.dsl.outcomes.Outcome
ir framework.outcomes.Rejection framework.dsl.outcomes.Rejection
ir framework.Domain$package$.UpTo framework.dsl.Domain$package$.UpTo
